<title>USA: INTELIDATA TO REPURCHASE SHARES.</title>
<headline>INTELIDATA TO REPURCHASE SHARES.</headline>
<dateline>HERNDON, Va. 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>InteliData Technologies Corp said on Tuesday that its directors had authorized a share buyback of up to two million shares on the open market.</p>
<p>&quot;While we have resisted using cash for a buyback of stock in the past, we feel that at the present trading range, it would be an excellent investment for the company,&quot; said InteliData president John Backus.</p>
<p>On August 6, the company said it did not expect to meet analysts' expectations for 1997. First Call consensus figures put the company's earnings for the year at $0.23 per share.</p>
<p>InteliData, which develops telecommunications products, recently posted a second quarter loss of $0.09 per share compared with a loss of $0.20 per share for the year-ago period.</p>
